536 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(The first version of the intake system used a simple intake box but had several flaws. It moved down using a virtual four-bar mechanism, keeping the intake\220s end effector parallel to the ground. However, this caused problems when pivoting, making movement inefficient. Samples frequently slipped out, there was no automated way to detect colors, and the horizontal sample orientation made it difficult for the claw to pick them up properly.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

537 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 273 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/A[981 0 R 0]/K[9]>>
endobj

538 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 273 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/A[898 0 R 0]/K[10]>>
endobj

539 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(CSK Develop3rs)/E(CSK Develop3rs)/Pg 17 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

540 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(Page 8)/E(Page 8)/Pg 17 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

541 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(23441)/E(23441)/Pg 17 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

542 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 273 0 R/T(Intake Iterations)/E(Intake Iterations)/Pg 17 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

543 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(Version 2:)/E(Version 2:)/Pg 17 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

544 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(Improvements included a front groove to prevent slipping, a color sensor for detection, and a vertical sample orientation for easier pickup. However, we still used the virtual four-bar mechanism, which continued to cause movement issues, restricting smooth turns. The servo intake was still slow and obstructed the claw\220s path during autonomous movement. While better than the first version, this design still struggled with reliable sample collection and overall system automation.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

545 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 273 0 R/T(Version 3:)/E(Version 3:)/Pg 17 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

546 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 273 0 R/E(The final design used a motor-driven belt with counter-rotating rollers and flexible tubing for smooth intake. Instead of the virtual four-bar, we opted to tilt the intake down and up at an angle, eliminating movement issues. A color sensor identified samples, closing a servo gate for correct ones and ejecting incorrect ones via additional rollers. The system\220s tilting mechanism and belt-driven movement significantly improved efficiency, speed, and automation.)/Pg 17 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

547 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 273 0 R/Pg 17 0 R/A[909 0 R 0]/K[19]>>
endobj

548 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 274 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[982 0 R 0]/K[0]>>
endobj

549 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 274 0 R/T(Version 1:)/E(Version 1:)/Pg 18 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

550 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 274 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[898 0 R 0]/K[2]>>
endobj

551 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 274 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[983 0 R 0]/K[3]>>
endobj

552 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 274 0 R/Pg 18 0 R/A[984 0 R 0]/K[4]>>
