575 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 275 0 R/E(The Orca is equipped with a variety of sensors that work together to ensure optimal performance. One important sensor is the color sensor, which helps identify and sort samples after they are collected. This sensor ensures that only the correct samples, based on the assigned alliance color, are gathered, preventing any mix-ups and improving efficiency. Additionally, the Orca uses two distance sensors, each capable of measuring up to two meters. These sensors assist with maneuvering during the autonomous stage by detecting the distance between the two of the corner frame walls, allowing us the line up perfectly with the high basket. The robot also has a magnet limit switch sensor attached to its linkage. This sensor makes sure the linkage stops at the right point, by detecting the magnetic field on a magnet attached to the linkage, ensuring they don\220t extend too much or too little, which is essential for accurate movement.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

576 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 275 0 R/T(CSK Develop3rs)/E(CSK Develop3rs)/Pg 19 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

577 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 275 0 R/T(Page 10)/E(Page 10)/Pg 19 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

578 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 275 0 R/E(Finally, encoders on the motors track rotation and speed, providing real-time data that helps control the robot\220s movement. This allows for precise, controlled motion and smoother operation. Together, these sensors enhance the Orca\220s ability to perform tasks accurately and efficiently, contributing to its overall functionality.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

