1377 0 obj
<</Title(After extensive research and testing, we determined that each cycle of collecting and depositing a sample into the high basket takes approximately 9 seconds. Based on these calculations, we estimate that we can score up to 13 samples during the tele-op period, yielding a total of 104 points. By refining our intake and outtake mechanisms, we aim to improve consistency, reduce cycle time, and maximize our scoring efficiency throughout the match.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1359 0 R/Next 1378 0 R>>
endobj

1378 0 obj
<</Title(Through additional calculations, we also determined that the process of collecting a sample, delivering it to the human player, converting it into a specimen, and depositing it onto the high rung takes approximately 15 seconds. This estimation allows us to score around eight specimens during the tele-op period, resulting in a total of 80 points. By optimizing efficiency and minimizing cycle times, we aim to maximize our scoring potential throughout the match.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1359 0 R/Prev 1377 0 R>>
endobj

1379 0 obj
<</Title(Based on our analysis, we prioritized sample-based scoring for its efficiency and higher point potential. However, if our alliance partners excel at sample scoring, we can switch to specimen-based scoring as needed. In autonomous, we focus on specimens since the observation zone is closer to the submersible than the basket, ensuring a more consistent strategy. This approach maximizes adaptability and scoring potential while helping us contribute to victory.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1360 0 R/Next 1393 0 R>>
endobj

1380 0 obj
<</Title(Endgame:)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1360 0 R/Prev 1394 0 R>>
endobj

