1397 0 obj
<</Title(The drivetrain features a parallel plate design, with motors placed at the center of the robot to ensure balanced weight distribution. These motors are positioned as low as possible to the ground, lowering the center of gravity, which significantly improves stability and reduces the chance of tipping during movement. Moreover, the motors are located opposite the vertical slides to create a counterbalancing effect. This arrangement helps maintain the robot's balance even when the vertical slides are fully extended, ensuring that the robot remains steady and reliable throughout various tasks on the field.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1387 0 R/Next 1398 0 R>>
endobj

1398 0 obj
<</Title(Additionally, the drivetrain\220s structure is built for efficiency, offering smoother movements and better control during high-speed maneuvers or complex tasks. To sum it up, our drivetrain is a grand part of our robot, and could not advance our robot without its design and functionality.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1387 0 R/Prev 1397 0 R>>
endobj

